  "summary": "Five preprints posted 24–26 November 2026 report memory-efficient tools for assembly, alignment, placement and RNA search.",
  "synthesis": "The five preprints share a focus on reducing memory footprint and computation time in sequence analysis at scale. Lash implements UltraLogLog, ExaLogLog and HyperMinHash sketches, reportedly 28–43% more memory-efficient than HyperLogLog for approximating microbial genome content. Gallifrey applies locally consistent de Bruijn graphs to fast PacBio HiFi draft assembly, reportedly more than six times faster than rust-mdbg with half the memory. Local wavefront alignment (lWFA) and bidirectional lBiWFA target exact local alignment while retaining O(sN) time and lowering memory use. gPlace is presented as a memory-bounded drop-in replacement for pplacer that yields identical placements. RNAhub2 adds prefiltering, parallelized searches and NAF compression to structure-based RNA homology searching. The common novelty is algorithmic: bounded or reduced resource use with reported preservation of exactness or compatibility with established tools.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
